  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Are panels and room dividers OECM-eligible under Agreement 2025-470?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. Office panels, room dividers, privacy screens, and modular partition systems in this collection are all covered under OECM Agreement 2025-470. Ontario school boards, hospitals, municipalities, colleges, and not-for-profits can purchase on an OECM purchase order. Call 1-800-835-9565 or email quotes@brantbusinessinteriors.com referencing the agreement."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "When should I use panels versus full-height dividers versus quiet-space pods?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Desk-mounted panels (roughly 24\u2033\u201348\u2033 high) reduce visual distraction and add a small amount of sound dampening between adjacent workstations \u2014 the default for open-plan benching. Full-height room dividers (floor to near-ceiling) create defined zones for departments, hot-desking neighbourhoods, or meeting areas without committing to drywall. Quiet-space pods (see our Quiet Spaces collection) are sealed acoustic enclosures for phone calls, focus work, or one-on-one meetings \u2014 the right pick when you need actual acoustic privacy, not just visual separation. Call 1-800-835-9565 to walk through which fits your floor plan."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do panel and divider installations work in an existing office?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "For an existing open-plan office, the flow is: quote \u2192 free 2D layout that marks panel positions, divider runs, and any clearance requirements \u2192 confirmed PO \u2192 on-site install coordinated with your facilities team. Desk-mounted panels typically install without disrupting the workstation; freestanding dividers and full-height systems are quoted with the install effort included so procurement can see the labour line. We deliver and install across Ontario from Peterborough."
        }
      }
    ]
  },
